                <pb facs="0776" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2741a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Third Secretary
                        of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-20T20:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1936—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. The United Press from London today says that “the Spanish Government in the
                    last few days has issued two decrees declaring a blockade of various coastal
                    areas but no foreign Power so far has recognized the blockade.”</p>
                <p>Telegraph briefly any information that you can discreetly obtain on this
                    subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
